   861                              <1> ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return AL = 0 if it
   862                              <1> ; was ')' and 2 if it was ']'. Brackets of both kinds count together;
   863                              <1> ; strings are stepped over whole. A NUL first ends the program (for '\' with
   864                              <1> ; no closer; anything else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets
