  1007                              <1> ; waitk. At a console: WaitForSingleObject on the input handle for the
  1008                              <1> ; time (EAX: 0 just looks, -1 is INFINITE), then ReadConsoleInputA for one
  1009                              <1> ; event. Only key-down events
  1010                              <1> ; count: their character, or for the left and right arrow keys (virtual
  1011                              <1> ; keys 25h and 27h, which have none) ^B and ^F. Anything else is passed
  1012                              <1> ; over, and the wait starts again with its whole time: so a wait can last
  1013                              <1> ; longer than asked by the time of the events passed over (a key-up comes
  1014                              <1> ; soon after its key-down), which the spec allows ("about n ms"), and no
  1015                              <1> ; clock is needed.
  1016                              <1> ; Input that is not a console (a pipe or a file) is read a byte at a time
  1017                              <1> ; with ReadFile, and only by a wait that is not just a look (a look would
  1018                              <1> ; eat the input); at its end the interpreter exits.
